## Revision 1 — what B8 caught and what changed

The first DRAFT was rejected on **R-DUPLICATE**, correctly. Two AC-4 cases
(`?from=ontem` and `?from=nao-e-uma-data`) asserted the identical observable
against inputs in the same equivalence class — both non-empty strings that die
on `isCalendarDate`'s leading regex, never reaching the calendar round-trip that
makes `2026-02-31` discriminative — and the second case seeded a four-Task
fixture no `expect` ever read. Any bug failing one failed the other identically.

The redundant case was replaced with `?from=` (the empty string), which is a
genuinely distinct defect mode and one the plan's own Task 1(a) names: *"An
absent parameter is never a filter — only `undefined` is skipped, never an empty
string coerced to 'no filter'."* An implementation gating on truthiness passes
every other AC-4 case and fails this one. Re-run after the fix: **19 failed, 1
passed**, unchanged in shape.

B8's audit note was also correct and is fixed above: the `EXISTING_TEST_COVERS`
row claimed 20 tests in `test/task-list-contract.test.ts:80-206`; the real count
is 17 executed cases in that range (the file runs 22 in total). The same round
number appears once in the APPROVED plan's `## Mandatory Reading` row for that
file. It is left as-is deliberately — an APPROVED artifact is not edited
mid-flight, and nothing gates on the count: the plan's Level 3 check is
`git diff --quiet -- test/task-list-contract.test.ts`, which asserts the file was
not modified at all.

